<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Nuceria Alfaterna</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 308 BCE (approx.) · capital Nuceria</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Oscan city of southern Campania that led a league including Pompeii, Herculaneum and Stabiae before becoming an ally of Rome.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nuceria Alfaterna, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nocera-inferiore">Nocera Inferiore</a>, grew in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarno-river">Sarno</a> valley inland from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>, on the route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-salerno">Gulf of Salerno</a>. Its population was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a>-speaking by the 5th century BCE, and earlier settlement shows Etruscan and Greek contacts.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nuceria headed a league of towns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarno-river">Sarno</a> valley and along the coast, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompeii">Pompeii</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herculaneum">Herculaneum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stabiae">Stabiae</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorrento">Surrentum</a>, and issued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a> with the name of the Alfaterni. It controlled a fertile plain producing grain, wine and fruit. Little else is known of its institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-samnite-war">Second Samnite War</a> Nuceria fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> but submitted in 308 BCE and became an ally on favourable terms. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> destroyed it in 216 BCE for staying loyal to Rome, and it was later rebuilt. In 59 CE a riot between Nucerians and Pompeians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompeii">Pompeii's</a> amphitheatre was recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nuceria-alfaterna.jpg" alt="Nuceria Alfaterna" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Poul Krogsgård · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nocera1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 308 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nuceria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Oscan polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oscan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nucerian League, Nuceria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-454&amp;focus=nuceria-alfaterna" aria-label="Nuceria Alfaterna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5040 723 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nuceria Alfaterna lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5360 979L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5360 979h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5360 979h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-454&amp;focus=nuceria-alfaterna">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

